(gen_random_uuid(), 'wellington', 'local_legend', 'Ngake and Whātaitai is the story to ask about', 'In Wellington, Ngake and Whātaitai is a useful lore thread. Māori tradition tells that Wellington''s harbour was once a lake sealed from the sea, home to two taniwha. Keep it as a sourced starting point, then let the surrounding place make the story tangible.', 'Lore source trail: Ngake and Whātaitai', '🗝️', null, '{"source": "https://eng.mataurangamaori.tki.org.nz/Support-materials/Te-Reo-Maori/Maori-Myths-Legends-and-Contemporary-Stories/Ngake-and-Whataitai-the-taniwha-of-Wellington-harbour"}'::jsonb, '{"accessed": "2026-08-02", "confidence": "documented", "profile": "local-expert-addons", "review_state": "source_checked", "rights": "original_lore_copy", "rights_review": "link_only_ok", "seed_kind": "story", "seed_title": "Ngake and Whātaitai", "wave": "2026-08"}'::jsonb, 'https://eng.mataurangamaori.tki.org.nz/Support-materials/Te-Reo-Maori/Maori-Myths-Legends-and-Contemporary-Stories/Ngake-and-Whataitai-the-taniwha-of-Wellington-harbour', 'cc0', 180, 'reference_only'),
